{"step_index":201,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T05:10:49Z","input_tokens":3438,"cache_read_tokens":38552,"output_tokens":4262,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe goal is to create a new, functional program within the \"programa perfecto\" folder, leveraging all existing program information. The structure must prioritize compatibility and safety for the target device (ZTE B866V2, Xview+). It should include only working, safe files, excluding incompatible ones and those requiring internal modifications or hardware changes. The structure will have subfolders such as \"1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR\\\" containing necessary ADB and fastboot tools.\n\n\nExamining the hardware specifications of the target device suggested compatibility with fastboot and adb protocols. Determined that the directory structure must include tools for both U-Boot fastboot (PID_0D02) and Recovery fastbootd (PID_4EE7) modes. Identified and listed necessary Amlogic DNL protocol tools, USB burning utilities, and file system utilities to be included in the appropriate subfolders.\n\n\nExamined the file structure further, determining specific drivers, firmware, and utilities to include within the defined subfolders. Identified the need for both ADBAppControl and the Amlogic USB driver installer, alongside specific firmware images. Crucially, the firmware directory must only include validated B866V2 images, excluding all B866F files and specific potentially unsafe images.\n\n\nThe program will offer a unified menu to manage device connections via ADB (USB, network), Fastboot (Bootloader, Recovery), MTP, and Amlogic DNL protocols. The menu will enable one-click ADB unlocking features. This includes Play Protect bypass settings and complete removal of specific bloatware packages detected on the target device.\n\n\nFocus shifted to identifying and disabling specific bloatware packages, including \"Megacable Core,\" \"Megacable Updat